{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-3222","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3663","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3664","text":": Cross-Cutting Governance for Agents"}]},{"id":"blk-3223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3665","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-3666","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3667","text":" capability family represents an agent's ability to "},{"id":"spn-3668","marks":["bold"],"text":"enforce policy, verify identity, emit telemetry, manage cost budgets, and escalate to humans"},{"id":"spn-3669","text":" — the cross-cutting governance concerns that apply to every other primitive."}]},{"id":"blk-3224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3670","text":"In the [&] Protocol, "},{"id":"spn-3671","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3672","text":" is the sixth primitive (cross-cutting over four cognitive + one sensorimotor):"}]},{"id":"blk-3225","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3673","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-3674","text":" — what the agent knows"}]}],"id":"blk-3226","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3675","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-3676","text":" — how the agent decides"}]}],"id":"blk-3228","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3677","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-3678","text":" — when things happen"}]}],"id":"blk-3230","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3679","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-3680","text":" — where things are"}]}],"id":"blk-3232","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3681","marks":["code"],"text":"&body"},{"id":"spn-3682","text":" — how the agent is instantiated in an environment (perception, action, affordance)"}]}],"id":"blk-3234","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3683","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3684","text":" — who is acting, under what rules, at what cost"}]}],"id":"blk-3236","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3685","text":"Unlike the five other primitives, which each model a distinct cognitive or sensorimotor domain, "},{"id":"spn-3686","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3687","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-3688","marks":["bold"],"text":"cross-cutting"},{"id":"spn-3689","text":". It does not exist in isolation — it wraps, constrains, and observes the others. Every "},{"id":"spn-3690","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-3691","text":" operation can emit telemetry. Every "},{"id":"spn-3692","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-3693","text":" decision can trigger escalation. Every "},{"id":"spn-3694","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-3695","text":" action can be identity-verified. Every "},{"id":"spn-3696","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-3697","text":" forecast can be budget-checked. Every "},{"id":"spn-3698","marks":["code"],"text":"&body"},{"id":"spn-3699","text":" action can be affordance-filtered and authorization-gated."}]},{"id":"blk-3239","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3700","text":"Why "},{"id":"spn-3701","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3702","text":" exists as a first-class primitive"}]},{"id":"blk-3240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3703","text":"Agent governance is the most underfunded and underspecified area of AI infrastructure. As of 2025, only $414M has been invested across all dedicated AI safety/governance startups — less than 5% of total AI security investment."}]},{"id":"blk-3241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3704","text":"Yet Gartner predicts 40% of agentic AI projects will be scrapped by 2027, primarily due to governance failures:"}]},{"id":"blk-3242","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3705","text":"agents that exceed cost budgets with no enforcement mechanism"}]}],"id":"blk-3243","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3706","text":"agents that impersonate other agents with no identity verification"}]}],"id":"blk-3245","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3707","text":"agents that make high-stakes decisions with no human escalation path"}]}],"id":"blk-3247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3708","text":"agents that operate opaquely with no telemetry or audit trail"}]}],"id":"blk-3249","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3709","text":"multi-agent systems where no one knows which agent did what"}]}],"id":"blk-3251","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3710","text":"These are not feature requests. They are "},{"id":"spn-3711","marks":["bold"],"text":"enterprise-blocking gaps"},{"id":"spn-3712","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-3254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3713","text":"Treating governance as a first-class capability — rather than an afterthought bolted onto application code — allows the protocol to express:"}]},{"id":"blk-3255","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3714","text":"that an agent has governance constraints at all"}]}],"id":"blk-3256","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3715","text":"what kind of governance it has (telemetry, escalation, identity)"}]}],"id":"blk-3258","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3716","text":"which provider implements each governance concern"}]}],"id":"blk-3260","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3717","text":"how governance composes with memory, reasoning, time, space, and body"}]}],"id":"blk-3262","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3718","text":"what events, budgets, and escalation rules are enforced"}]}],"id":"blk-3264","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3719","text":"Without "},{"id":"spn-3720","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3721","text":", governance tends to be hidden inside ad hoc middleware, provider-specific plugins, or manual compliance processes. The result is architecture that works in demos but fails in production."}]},{"id":"blk-3267","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3722","text":"What "},{"id":"spn-3723","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3724","text":" means in the protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-3268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3725","text":"At the protocol level, "},{"id":"spn-3726","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3727","text":" is not a vendor, dashboard, or compliance tool."}]},{"id":"blk-3269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3728","text":"It is a "},{"id":"spn-3729","marks":["bold"],"text":"capability interface family"},{"id":"spn-3730","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-3270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3731","text":"That means:"}]},{"id":"blk-3271","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3732","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"},{"id":"spn-3733","text":" is a protocol capability"}]}],"id":"blk-3272","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3734","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience"},{"id":"spn-3735","text":" is one provider that may satisfy it"}]}],"id":"blk-3274","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3736","text":"another provider could also satisfy "},{"id":"spn-3737","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"},{"id":"spn-3738","text":" if it implements the same contract"}]}],"id":"blk-3276","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3739","text":"This separation is important."}]},{"id":"blk-3279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3740","text":"If governance were modeled only as provider-specific configuration, then changing your observability stack would require rewriting your agent declarations. By modeling "},{"id":"spn-3741","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3742","text":" as an interface family, the protocol stays portable."}]},{"id":"blk-3280","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3743","text":"Common "},{"id":"spn-3744","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3745","text":" subtypes"}]},{"id":"blk-3281","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3746","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"}]},{"id":"blk-3282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3747","text":"Represents the observability backbone: structured event emission, metric queries, and budget enforcement."}]},{"id":"blk-3283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3748","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-3284","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3749","text":"emitting structured telemetry events (OpenTelemetry-compatible)"}]}],"id":"blk-3285","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3750","text":"tracking token consumption and cost per task and per period"}]}],"id":"blk-3287","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3290","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3751","text":"enforcing budget limits from Delegatic policy trees"}]}],"id":"blk-3289","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3752","text":"querying historical telemetry for audit and analysis"}]}],"id":"blk-3291","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3753","text":"detecting anomalous agent behavior via cost or usage patterns"}]}],"id":"blk-3293","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3754","text":"This is the subtype most relevant to cost management, observability, and compliance."}]},{"id":"blk-3296","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3755","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.escalation"}]},{"id":"blk-3297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3756","text":"Represents the human-in-the-loop bridge: structured handoff from autonomous operation to human review."}]},{"id":"blk-3298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3757","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-3299","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3758","text":"escalating when confidence falls below a threshold"}]}],"id":"blk-3300","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3759","text":"escalating when cost exceeds a budget"}]}],"id":"blk-3302","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3760","text":"escalating when a hard governance boundary is approached"}]}],"id":"blk-3304","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3761","text":"escalating when policy explicitly requires human approval"}]}],"id":"blk-3306","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3762","text":"tracking escalation history and response patterns"}]}],"id":"blk-3308","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3763","text":"This subtype matters whenever autonomous operation must have a safety valve."}]},{"id":"blk-3311","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3764","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.identity"}]},{"id":"blk-3312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3765","text":"Represents cross-runtime agent identity: verification, registration, and trust."}]},{"id":"blk-3313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3766","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-3314","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3767","text":"verifying that an agent is who it claims to be (manifest hash, spec hash)"}]}],"id":"blk-3315","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3768","text":"registering agent identity on publish or deployment"}]}],"id":"blk-3317","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3769","text":"resolving agent identity from an ID or manifest reference"}]}],"id":"blk-3319","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3770","text":"preventing agent impersonation in multi-agent systems"}]}],"id":"blk-3321","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3771","text":"associating governance policies with verified identities"}]}],"id":"blk-3323","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3325","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3772","text":"This subtype is essential for multi-agent systems where trust between agents is not assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-3326","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3773","text":"Future subtype candidates"}]},{"id":"blk-3327","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3774","text":"As the protocol evolves, additional governance subtypes may emerge:"}]},{"id":"blk-3328","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3775","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.audit"},{"id":"spn-3776","text":" — dedicated audit trail management"}]}],"id":"blk-3329","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3777","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.consent"},{"id":"spn-3778","text":" — user consent and data governance"}]}],"id":"blk-3331","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3779","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.compliance"},{"id":"spn-3780","text":" — regulatory compliance checks"}]}],"id":"blk-3333","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3781","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.rate_limit"},{"id":"spn-3782","text":" — fine-grained rate limiting per capability"}]}],"id":"blk-3335","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3783","text":"The protocol should stay conservative at the primitive level and extensible at the subtype level."}]},{"id":"blk-3338","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3784","text":"What problems "},{"id":"spn-3785","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3786","text":" solves"}]},{"id":"blk-3339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3787","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3788","text":" gives the protocol a standard place to express capabilities like:"}]},{"id":"blk-3340","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3789","text":"tracking what every agent does and what it costs"}]}],"id":"blk-3341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3790","text":"enforcing budget limits across an org hierarchy"}]}],"id":"blk-3343","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3791","text":"verifying agent identity before allowing collaboration"}]}],"id":"blk-3345","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3792","text":"escalating to humans when confidence or cost thresholds are crossed"}]}],"id":"blk-3347","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3793","text":"auditing the full provenance chain of a decision"}]}],"id":"blk-3349","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3794","text":"detecting and preventing adversarial behavior (OS-007)"}]}],"id":"blk-3351","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3795","text":"These are especially important when agents operate autonomously, at scale, across organizational boundaries."}]},{"id":"blk-3354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3796","text":"Example:"}]},{"id":"blk-3355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3797","text":"A fleet management agent optimizes delivery routes. Without "},{"id":"spn-3798","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3799","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-3356","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3800","text":"No one knows how many tokens it consumed this month"}]}],"id":"blk-3357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3801","text":"No one can verify it's the same agent that was tested and approved"}]}],"id":"blk-3359","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3802","text":"If it encounters an edge case it can't handle, it either hallucinates or fails silently"}]}],"id":"blk-3361","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3803","text":"If it exceeds the cost budget, there's no enforcement mechanism"}]}],"id":"blk-3363","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3804","text":"With "},{"id":"spn-3805","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry + &govern.identity + &govern.escalation"},{"id":"spn-3806","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-3366","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3807","text":"Every route optimization emits a telemetry event with token count and cost"}]}],"id":"blk-3367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3808","text":"The agent's identity is verified against its FleetPrompt manifest on deployment"}]}],"id":"blk-3369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3809","text":"When confidence drops below 0.6, it escalates to a human dispatcher"}]}],"id":"blk-3371","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3810","text":"When cost exceeds "},{"id":"spn-3811","marks":["code"],"text":"max_cost_usd_per_task"},{"id":"spn-3812","text":", the operation is rejected with a clear budget error"}]}],"id":"blk-3373","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3375","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3813","text":"How "},{"id":"spn-3814","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3815","text":" differs from the governance block"}]},{"id":"blk-3376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3816","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-3817","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-3818","text":" "},{"id":"spn-3819","marks":["code"],"text":"governance"},{"id":"spn-3820","text":" block declares "},{"id":"spn-3821","marks":["bold"],"text":"what rules apply"},{"id":"spn-3822","text":" (hard constraints, soft preferences, escalation thresholds)."}]},{"id":"blk-3377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3823","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-3824","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3825","text":" capability declares "},{"id":"spn-3826","marks":["bold"],"text":"which systems enforce those rules"},{"id":"spn-3827","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-3378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3828","text":"They are complementary:"}]},{"id":"blk-3379","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&govern.telemetry\": {\n      \"provider\": \"opensentience\",\n      \"config\": { \"org_id\": \"org_acme\" }\n    },\n    \"&govern.escalation\": {\n      \"provider\": \"opensentience\",\n      \"config\": { \"timeout_seconds\": 300 }\n    }\n  },\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"hard\": [\"Never exceed $50 per task\"],\n    \"escalate_when\": {\n      \"confidence_below\": 0.7,\n      \"cost_exceeds_usd\": 50\n    },\n    \"autonomy\": {\n      \"level\": \"advise\",\n      \"budget\": {\n        \"max_cost_usd_per_task\": 50,\n        \"max_tokens_per_period\": 1000000\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-3380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3829","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-3830","marks":["code"],"text":"governance"},{"id":"spn-3831","text":" block is the "},{"id":"spn-3832","marks":["bold"],"text":"policy declaration"},{"id":"spn-3833","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-3834","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3835","text":" capabilities are the "},{"id":"spn-3836","marks":["bold"],"text":"enforcement mechanisms"},{"id":"spn-3837","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-3381","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3838","text":"How "},{"id":"spn-3839","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3840","text":" composes with the other primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-3382","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3841","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3842","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-3843","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"}]},{"id":"blk-3383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3844","text":"Every memory operation can emit telemetry. Memory consolidation cycles can be budget-checked. Knowledge graph mutations can trigger identity verification for the writing agent."}]},{"id":"blk-3384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3845","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-3385","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3846","text":"tracking which agent wrote which knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-3386","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3847","text":"enforcing storage budgets"}]}],"id":"blk-3388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3848","text":"auditing knowledge provenance"}]}],"id":"blk-3390","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3392","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3849","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3850","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-3851","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"}]},{"id":"blk-3393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3852","text":"Every deliberation can be cost-tracked. High-stakes decisions can trigger escalation. Voting agents can be identity-verified before participating."}]},{"id":"blk-3394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3853","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-3395","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3854","text":"budget-bounded deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-3396","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3855","text":"human review of critical decisions"}]}],"id":"blk-3398","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3856","text":"preventing impersonation in multi-agent voting"}]}],"id":"blk-3400","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3402","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3857","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3858","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-3859","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"}]},{"id":"blk-3403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3860","text":"Temporal forecasts and anomaly detections can emit telemetry. Expensive SSM inference can be budget-checked. Anomaly thresholds can trigger escalation when they exceed governance bounds."}]},{"id":"blk-3404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3861","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-3405","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3862","text":"cost tracking for temporal intelligence operations"}]}],"id":"blk-3406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3863","text":"degraded-mode fallback when compute budget is exhausted"}]}],"id":"blk-3408","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3864","text":"human review of high-impact temporal predictions"}]}],"id":"blk-3410","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3412","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3865","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3866","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-3867","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"}]},{"id":"blk-3413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3868","text":"Route optimizations can emit telemetry with compute cost. Geofence boundary crossings can trigger escalation. Fleet operations agents can be identity-verified before accessing sensitive location data."}]},{"id":"blk-3414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3869","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-3415","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3870","text":"spatial operation cost tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-3416","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3871","text":"compliance escalation on boundary violations"}]}],"id":"blk-3418","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3872","text":"identity-gated access to fleet data"}]}],"id":"blk-3420","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3422","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3873","text":"Full composition: all six primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-3423","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n  |> &time.anomaly.detect()\n  |> &govern.telemetry.emit()\n  |> &space.fleet.enrich()\n  |> &govern.telemetry.budget_check()\n  |> &memory.graph.enrich()\n  |> &reason.argument.evaluate()\n  |> &body.browser.affordances()     # policy-filtered action set\n  |> &govern.escalation.authorize()  # authorize destructive body actions\n  |> &body.browser.act()\n  |> &govern.escalation.escalate()   # if confidence < threshold"},{"id":"blk-3424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3874","text":"This pipeline shows how "},{"id":"spn-3875","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3876","text":" weaves through the other five primitives — not as a separate stage, but as an observability and enforcement layer that accompanies every operation, including "},{"id":"spn-3877","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-3878","text":" affordance filtering and action authorization."}]},{"id":"blk-3425","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3879","text":"Typical providers"}]},{"id":"blk-3426","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3880","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience"}]},{"id":"blk-3427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3881","text":"The primary runtime enforcement provider. Implements:"}]},{"id":"blk-3428","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3882","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim (permission engine, lifecycle, autonomy levels)"}]}],"id":"blk-3429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3883","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness (identity verification, budget enforcement, circuit breakers)"}]}],"id":"blk-3431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3884","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness (pipeline enforcement, quality gates, sprint contracts, context management)"}]}],"id":"blk-3433","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3435","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3885","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-3436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3886","text":"The policy source provider. Provides:"}]},{"id":"blk-3437","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3887","text":"Monotonic policy inheritance (budget limits flow from root to leaf orgs)"}]}],"id":"blk-3438","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3888","text":"Budget fields: "},{"id":"spn-3889","marks":["code"],"text":"max_tokens_per_task"},{"id":"spn-3890","text":", "},{"id":"spn-3891","marks":["code"],"text":"max_cost_usd_per_period"},{"id":"spn-3892","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-3440","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3893","text":"Policy merge semantics: AND for booleans, MIN for numerics, INTERSECTION for allow-lists"}]}],"id":"blk-3442","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3444","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3894","marks":["code"],"text":"fleetprompt"}]},{"id":"blk-3445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3895","text":"The identity registry provider. Provides:"}]},{"id":"blk-3446","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3896","text":"Agent manifest registration on publish"}]}],"id":"blk-3447","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3897","text":"Identity verification for marketplace agents"}]}],"id":"blk-3449","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3898","text":"Trust score computation from test coverage + spec compliance + usage history"}]}],"id":"blk-3451","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3453","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3899","text":"Anti-patterns"}]},{"id":"blk-3454","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3900","text":"Anti-pattern 1: Treating governance as optional"}]},{"id":"blk-3455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3901","text":"If an agent operates autonomously, governance is not optional. Skipping "},{"id":"spn-3902","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3903","text":" declarations doesn't remove governance concerns — it just makes them invisible."}]},{"id":"blk-3456","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3904","text":"Anti-pattern 2: Hardcoding budget limits in application code"}]},{"id":"blk-3457","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3905","text":"Budget limits should flow from Delegatic policy trees, not be hardcoded per agent. Use "},{"id":"spn-3906","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry.budget_check()"},{"id":"spn-3907","text":" against the policy tree."}]},{"id":"blk-3458","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3908","text":"Anti-pattern 3: Identity verification only at deploy time"}]},{"id":"blk-3459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3909","text":"Agent identity should be verified continuously — not just when first deployed. Use "},{"id":"spn-3910","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.identity.verify()"},{"id":"spn-3911","text":" before accepting collaboration requests."}]},{"id":"blk-3460","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3912","text":"Anti-pattern 4: Escalation as error handling"}]},{"id":"blk-3461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3913","text":"Escalation is a governance-mandated handoff, not an error. Design escalation paths as first-class workflows, not exception handlers."}]},{"id":"blk-3462","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3914","text":"Anti-pattern 5: Telemetry without structured schemas"}]},{"id":"blk-3463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3915","text":"Unstructured log messages are not telemetry. Use the OpenTelemetry-compatible event schema with typed fields (trace_id, agent_id, capability, tokens_consumed, cost_usd_estimated)."}]},{"id":"blk-3464","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-3916","text":"Summary"}]},{"id":"blk-3465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3917","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3918","text":" is the protocol's answer to the question:"}]},{"id":"blk-3466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3919","marks":["bold"],"text":"How does an agent operate safely, transparently, and within bounds?"}]},{"id":"blk-3467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3920","text":"It matters because autonomous agents without governance are demos, not products."}]},{"id":"blk-3468","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3921","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3922","text":" makes governance:"}]},{"id":"blk-3469","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3923","text":"explicit in the declaration"}]}],"id":"blk-3470","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3924","text":"separable from providers"}]}],"id":"blk-3472","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3925","text":"contract-aware"}]}],"id":"blk-3474","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3926","text":"composable with memory, time, space, and reason"}]}],"id":"blk-3476","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3927","text":"enforceable"}]}],"id":"blk-3478","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3928","text":"auditable"}]}],"id":"blk-3480","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-3483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3929","text":"compilable into downstream agent artifacts"}]}],"id":"blk-3482","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-3484","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3930","text":"If "},{"id":"spn-3931","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-3932","text":" helps the agent remember, and "},{"id":"spn-3933","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-3934","text":" helps it decide, and "},{"id":"spn-3935","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-3936","text":" helps it understand change, and "},{"id":"spn-3937","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-3938","text":" helps it stay grounded in the world,"}]},{"id":"blk-3485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-3939","text":"then "},{"id":"spn-3940","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-3941","text":" ensures it does all of that "},{"id":"spn-3942","marks":["bold"],"text":"safely, transparently, and within the rules"},{"id":"spn-3943","text":"."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieramgbpsk7fsppaqx3vkfvx55lehvrwwewnsyv545b7avkhdrsi3oaq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}